    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d244">

                <pb facs="0403" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg303"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/113</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 855 Political</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-27">March 27, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        4.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit the original
                    of a communication addressed to the Secretary of State under date of March 22,
                    1934 from the Secretary-General of the High Commission for Refugees coming from
                        Germany,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d244-f1"/> stating that the next meeting of
                    the Governing Body of the High Commission will be held in London on May 2 and 3,
                    1934.</p>
                <p>This communication also encloses a copy of a letter<anchor n="5" xml:id="d244-f2"
                    /> addressed by the Secretary-General of the Commission to Professor Joseph P.
                    Chamberlain, setting forth the agenda of the meeting in question.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prentiss B.
                    Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
